# For Smoother SRB Flames (the hooks' SrbFlames.cs): the trail march and the volume caches, which sample a segment with
# the same function, fade a moving trail segment's motion out within 60 m of the eye. The game's trail segments never
# move (only explosions do, on paths and in code of their own), so the fade only ever meets the motion SrbFlames gives
# the hot exhaust riding with the followed vessel: kept whole, the flames close to the camera keep their history too.

@@ edit srb-flames VolumetricTrail/TrailProfileSampling.glsl
@@ what the trail segments' motion kept near the eye
@@ find
    vec3 previousAxisOffset = (previousAxisPoint - axisPoint) *
        smoothstep(0.0, SEGMENT_MOTION_NEAR_FADE_DISTANCE, length(position));
@@ replace
    // macOS port: Smoother SRB Flames. Not faded near the eye, whatever the game's comment above says: its trails stand
    // still, so the only motion here is the hot exhaust's that the hooks give, riding with the followed vessel
    vec3 previousAxisOffset = previousAxisPoint - axisPoint;
